[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Austrian Defense"]
[ECO "D06"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "open-the-centre"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2...c5"]
[Start "orthodox 2.c4"]

2... c5 3. cxd5 { Opens the c-file and clears the way for the knight on c3 to hit the queen. } 3... Qxd5 ( 3... cxd4 4. Qxd4 { Takes back with the queen. White is a pawn up for now: Black's queen cannot take on d5 while White's queen guards it. } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. e4 { Takes the centre. If Black takes on d5, White's pieces come out quickly against the open king. } ) 4. Nf3 { Develops and prepares Nc3 so White gains time on the queen. } 4... cxd4 ( 4... Nc6 5. Nc3 { Hits the queen again. } 5... Qd6 6. d5 { Chases the knight and takes space. Black has lost a lot of time with the queen. } ) 5. Nc3 { Hits the queen and gains time. } 5... Qa5 6. Nxd4 { Takes the pawn back with a developing move. } 6... Nf6 7. Nb3 { Hits the queen again and steps away from the pin and from exchanges. } 7... Qc7 8. e4 { Takes the centre now that Black has wasted time on the queen. Plan: develop the bishops, castle, and keep the pawns on e4 and d-file open. } *
